# Git: parent workspace + le-wm submodule

Two repositories. Edits in the wrong one (or a bump of the wrong SHA) are the
usual failure mode.

Local identity (both repos, **not** global): `user.name=yojuna`,
`user.email=datamongeraami@gmail.com`. SSH for `git@github.com:` in these
repos is `core.sshCommand` → `~/.ssh/yojuna_ed25519` (Host `github.com` in
`~/.ssh/config` is a different GitHub account).

## Repos

**Parent** (`ws_weltmodelle/`): branch `main`.
`origin` = `git@github.com:yojuna/ws_weltmodelle.git`. Owns `docker/`, `docs/`,
`README.md`, `.gitignore`, `.gitmodules`, `wiki/`, and **`ws_le-wm/docs/`**.
Records the submodule as a gitlink (`160000`) at `ws_le-wm/le-wm`.

**Submodule** (`ws_le-wm/le-wm/`): all Python, Hydra configs, `scripts/`,
`thresholds.yaml`.

| Remote | URL | Use |
|--------|-----|-----|
| `origin` | `git@github.com:yojuna/le-wm.git` | Our fork. Push `feat/lewm-phi` here. |
| `upstream` | `https://github.com/lucas-maes/le-wm.git` | Author repo. `git fetch upstream` then merge/rebase onto `main`. |

Work branch: `feat/lewm-phi` (tracks `origin/feat/lewm-phi`). `main` tracks
`upstream/main`.

```bash
git clone --recurse-submodules git@github.com:yojuna/ws_weltmodelle.git
git submodule update --init --recursive   # if cloned without --recurse
```

## Where to commit

| Change | Commit in |
|--------|-----------|
| `ws_le-wm/le-wm/**` (code, configs, tests) | **submodule first**, then `git push origin feat/lewm-phi` |
| `ws_le-wm/docs/**`, `docker/`, `docs/`, README | **parent**, then `git push origin main` |
| After a submodule commit | parent: `git add ws_le-wm/le-wm` (bump SHA) |

Do not put research docs inside the submodule. Do not copy le-wm out of the
submodule or treat the parent tree as a single repo when staging.

Typical parent messages: `Bump le-wm: <why>.` or `Record <result> and bump le-wm.`
Submodule: imperative, what landed (`Add smear-structure eval: …`).

## Do not

- `git push` the submodule to `upstream` (`lucas-maes/le-wm`) unless asked.
- Commit gitignored artifacts (`eval_results/` dumps, `*.ckpt`, `*.pt`, `wandb/`,
  `docker/.venv/`, `**/stablewm/checkpoints|datasets|videos/`). Small metric
  JSON may already be force-added; do not mass-add `eval_results/`.
- Amend, force-push, or skip hooks unless asked.
- Use the work global identity (`haverboecker`) on these repos.

After code+docs work, `git status` in **both** repos; parent should show a
submodule SHA change when the submodule moved.
